    "source": "sneed 2026-11-27 (stamina: a 100 bar, light 10, heavy 20, a blocked hit half its attack's cost, a roll 30, refills over 2 s of no use, a raised guard stops the refill) and Elden Ring's shape as players measured it (poise refills 30 s after the last hit, light/heavy/charged stance damage about 1 : 1.6 : 2.4, running, jumping, rolling attacks and guard counters; critical attacks about 3x a normal blow, ripostes about 25% above backstabs); the rest ours (docs/design/souls-combat.md). sneed 2026-11-28: a committed opening after a chain (openingSteps), grounded heavies and a straight leap, a smaller carry-in. sneed 2026-11-28 (tactical): poise 10, a weak hit takes 2 and a strong one 6 (weaponPoise 2 times the kind's poise), at 0 it resets and can't break again for 10 s (poiseImmuneSteps); any hit on a foe whose poise broke is the riposte (the impale), fast, the foe held then staggering; swings 25% slower (moveset speed 0.75); a real recovery before the next blow (chainShare 0.45) and a press during the wind-up is too early (earlyPressBreaksChain); a blow on a guard adds 0.15 s to both sides' next attack (blockedDelaySteps); a raised shield keeps bodies 0.8 m off (shieldRoom). enabled false turns all of it off and melee is what it was. sneed 2026-11-28 (combos): press again during a swing and the next blow follows right after it (chainShare 0.1, presses in the wind-up kept: earlyPressBreaksChain false); the player's grounded sword attacks stay where they are with the feet free (playerStaysPut); the jumping heavy is a fast grounded chop with no air time (Motion_SS_HeavyDown at 1.6), the jump attack a lunging slash (Motion_SS_Attack3). sneed 2026-11-28 (running lunges: make it so they run into you and add a lunging attack while running, all weapons, they don't stop running until you do; a lunging attack is -6 poise): Running poise 3 (6 with weaponPoise 2), the lunge* numbers (ours), and a lungeOnly moveset per weapon kind still on the old swing (one hand, dual wield, two hand, the spear's impale, fists).",
